  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative launched in Q3 2023, led by Marcus Cole, aimed at enhancing security and accessibility. The project has undergone team expansions, adding five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, as well as Mike Chen and Lisa Ray for machine learning and cloud computing. A partnership with TechInnovate to leverage AI technology is being explored. Security protocols were updated in January to include multi-factor authentication and encryption. The compliance plan budget was increased to $55,000, and a separate training budget of $15,000 was approved for coding teams and project managers. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience was requested by the end of November, and a detailed assessment of similar projects was recommended to position offerings effectively."
